TOOLKIT=$(PROGRAMFILES)\Civ4SDK\Microsoft Visual C++ Toolkit 2003
PSDK=$(PROGRAMFILES)\Civ4SDK\WindowsSDK
CIV4_PATH=$(PROGRAMFILES)\Steam\steamapps\common\Sid Meier's Civilization IV Beyond the Sword
#
# <!-- custom: note with the help of chatgpt thanks, also note below that Civ4Libs folder is just an example, it could be any folder name other than "Civ4Libs" and path other than program files if you prefer as long as it has the required Boost 1.32.0 and Python24 folders (and their files obviously not just empty folders), just i wanted them to be outside of git so that it doesn't clutter and in case we do manual backups too as i do quite some/many times. -->
# CIV4_LIB_INSTALL_PATH is not set here.
# Instead, it should be defined as a Windows environment variable.
# Example (permanent):
#   System Properties → Environment Variables → Add:
#     Name: CIV4_LIB_INSTALL_PATH
#     Value: C:\Program Files (x86)\Civ4Libs
# This is where Boost 1.32.0 and Python24 headers/libs must be placed.
#
# <!-- custom: note 1 also: i have not renamed mod name to AdvCiv-SAS in compiler files and such as may cause unexpected errors and our mod is fundamentally based on advciv mod so name is close enough, but the DLL is generated based on our real source files not base advciv ones i mean, just i am careful in this case to rather not rename mod name in compiler files or and such settings at least as of now, may change this later or maybe not since runs fine and does not seem to cause issues -->
#
# <!-- custom: note 2: before compiling, delete the exact temp_files/<target> folder for that configuration so the accepted DLL cannot resume from stale or partial fastdep intermediates; see the AdvCiv-SAS DLL Compilation Guide and Known Issues. A successful Debug-opt folder may then be retained until its next build because its exact matching PDB makes crash dumps actionable. Target folders are isolated, so retained Debug-opt symbols do not affect a clean Release build. (GPT-5.6-Sol) -->
